    {
      "id": "claim_2e40b7c4004347399b542678bc02efc3",
      "statement": "A hibernated cell keeps no memory across the resident to dormant transition, so the next event runs the object's constructor again exactly as a cold start does; the surviving hibernatable WebSocket clients and the node it stays on are the only difference from Inactive.",
      "evidence": [
